    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "block-sparse-mlp",
        "title": "Restore the native routing call contract",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "The entire edit removes one positional False from BlockSparseMLP.forward. Whole-parent search finds this as the sole Python call to blocksparse_mlp_routing; its declaration and binding remain unchanged.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_4fe7f9c7606741fbb0abae986c908a1b",
              "call_aadac5dbd51f47e093fcd87ea5b0aae0",
              "call_1ce9fed7d73246388a9a6cc3e21f1645",
              "call_7a3f6621e1fd434ca79b4947736c868f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The native router multiplies flattened token rows by the gate matrix, selects expert logits and softmax-normalizes the selected values. One token without all-expert activation reuses configured output buffers; other cases allocate results and select either the configured expert count or every expert. It returns indices followed by weights.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_d0d382ff63034220bf89a3197c9b85b1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Routing occurs before the ordinary-versus-fused expert dispatch, so the argument repair applies to both paths. The ordinary path handles multiple flattened tokens or non-fully-EXL3 experts; the fused path handles one token with fully EXL3 experts. The threshold 1 is a token-count dispatch condition, not a newly tuned performance threshold.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_e5b969b808f247e38d3cf80adfea8878",
              "call_4fe7f9c7606741fbb0abae986c908a1b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Repository construction sites are Mixtral, Qwen3 MoE and Dots1. TransformerBlock forwards params to its MLP and immediately consumes the result in residual addition. ParallelDecoderBlock has another generic MLP call, but its declared constructor types exclude BlockSparseMLP; this is not evidence of a registered sparse-model workflow there.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_630a4b1e94f14d0e9e8574a13c508db5",
              "call_9c8c59743f5b4bf797cf149d6b5c4b38",
              "call_db7d0d84c39c433caa6b47c2121c56cd",
              "call_fdb5e32bb15d4f47b8dd5bf27b31f20d",
              "call_8bf8287596514c09b56db8bd6d102d26"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The author's \u201cFix regression\u201d description is consistent with restoring the previously documented native interface. It does not imply that all conditional BlockSparseMLP paths now succeed: grouped routing, optional Dots inputs and fused-output contracts remain unchanged.",
            "basis": "inference",
            "evidence": [
              "call_4fe7f9c7606741fbb0abae986c908a1b",
              "call_33a2395a1305486daa293943b378e412",
              "call_e5b969b808f247e38d3cf80adfea8878"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
